sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  actor User
  participant SPA as React SPA
  participant API as Django API
  participant MW as APIKeyMiddleware
  participant DRF as APIKeyAuthentication
  participant Cache as Django cache
  participant DB as PostgreSQL

  User->>SPA: Create API key
  SPA->>API: POST /api/v1/auth/api-keys/ with JWT
  API->>DB: Store SHA-256 digest in UserAPIKey.key_hash
  API-->>SPA: Return raw key once

  User->>SPA: Call protected API
  SPA->>API: HTTPS + X-API-Key
  API->>MW: Apply path allowlist
  MW->>Cache: Lookup key digest cache
  alt Cache hit
    Cache-->>MW: UserAPIKey record ID
    MW->>DB: Load active key/user
  else Cache miss
    MW->>DB: Query UserAPIKey.key_hash
    DB-->>MW: Matching key record
    MW->>Cache: Cache key record ID for five minutes
  end
  MW->>DRF: Continue request with user context
  DRF->>Cache: Check API-key auth cache
  alt Middleware populated cache
    Cache-->>DRF: Key record ID
    DRF-->>API: Authenticated user
  else Direct DRF database fallback
    DRF->>DB: Query hashed_key field
    DB-->>DRF: Field does not exist on UserAPIKey model
    DRF-->>API: Authentication failure on this path
  end
  API-->>SPA: View response or 401

  User->>SPA: Revoke key
  SPA->>API: DELETE /api/v1/auth/api-keys/{id}/
  API->>DB: Mark key inactive
  API-->>SPA: Revocation response

  Note over API,DB: No API-key scopes and no legal acceptance gate are implemented.
